  "platform": "Sega Mega Drive / Genesis",
  "summary": "Streets of Rage 3 is Sega's side-scrolling fighting game for Mega Drive, first released in Japan on 18 March 1994 as Bare Knuckle III.",
  "body": [
    "Streets of Rage 3 is Sega's side-scrolling fighting game for Mega Drive, first released in Japan on 18 March 1994 as Bare Knuckle III. Axel, Blaze and Skate return alongside Dr. Zan, a scientist with a mechanical body. Their investigation brings them into another scheme involving Mr. X and robotic replacements for public figures. One or two players fight through streets and buildings, clearing groups of attackers before moving onwards. The familiar procession of punches, throws and improvised weapons now gives the fighters more ways to keep moving.",
    "Every character can run and roll vertically across the screen. These movements help close a gap, escape a surrounding group or approach an enemy from another line. Special attacks draw on a rechargeable meter: using one when the meter is full avoids the usual health cost. Waiting for that opportunity makes the attack a resource to manage during a crowded fight. Weapons wear out through use, while Zan changes the way found weapons behave by converting them into energy attacks suited to his mechanical body.",
    "The journey can reach different endings depending on decisions and performance during the later stages. That gives the rescue and pursuit a consequence beyond reaching the next boss. The Japanese and Western editions also differ in presentation, story details and difficulty, so the same title can recall rather different experiences. Yuzo Koshiro and Motohiro Kawashima returned to compose the soundtrack. Their increasingly experimental electronic music accompanies a sequel whose faster movement and expanded combat push the series further than its outwardly familiar streets first suggest."
  ],
  "story_headings": [
    "Back on the streets",
    "Keeping the fight moving",
    "A changing investigation"
  ],
